mtkclient v2.1.4.1 (commit 5a863eece86fcaa97cb8325cf747e0aae3c307e4): fixes for the macOS serial
driver (--serialport), applied by 'toque-setup.sh prepare' and checked before every download-mode
step. Found on a real Monsieur Cuisine Connect (MT6580 preloader) on 2026-11-15; without them the
preloader handshake ends in "Sync error" and the DA upload stops half-way.

1. Port.run_serial_handshake: the preloader sends "READY" as soon as its port opens. Those bytes
   were read as handshake echoes, shifting every later reply. Drain the input before the handshake
   and after each mismatch. Reported as bkerler/mtkclient#458 (not fixed upstream as of 2026-11).
2. SerialClass.usbread: with no timeout given (e.g. a DA ACK), wait up to the class default (1 s)
   instead of 20 ms.
3. SerialClass.write / flush: pyserial's flushOutput() is reset_output_buffer(), which discards
   bytes not yet sent (tcflush TCOFLUSH): the DA then waits forever for the end of a packet. Use
   flush() (tcdrain). Fixed upstream after v2.1.4.1 (bkerler/mtkclient#367).

